<title>UK: RESEARCH ALERT - IMI cut to &quot;hold&quot; at CSFB.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT - IMI cut to &quot;hold&quot; at CSFB.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian investment bank IMI was cut to &quot;hold&quot; from &quot;buy&quot; at CS First Boston, the investment bank said on Friday.</p>
<p>CSFB said persistant &quot;strategic weaknesses&quot; at IMI were becoming accentuated. It said the acquisition of a branch network was becoming &quot;all but inevitable,&quot; suggesting that excess capital was not likely to be returned to shareholders.</p>
<p>The stock was down 380 lire at 15,560 by 1010 GMT.</p>
<p>-- David Holmes, London Newsroom +44 171 542 4367</p>
</text>
